#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1072 expect=noViolation domain=RELREC
#note "Copy of valid-RELREC with row 2 RDOMAIN = dm: Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner, queued item C3, as c5206c02): RDOMAIN names a domain, and dataset names match case-insensitively (owner 2026-10-01), so the literal comparison reads upper(RDOMAIN). The DM exception still applies, so the empty IDVAR is allowed -> no violation. Red under the old exact comparison (dm != DM fired)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset RELREC label="Related Records"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col RELID    type=Char label="Relationship Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | AESEQ | 1 | REL1
CDISCPILOT01 | dm | 01-701-1015 |       |   | REL2
CDISCPILOT01 |    | 01-701-1015 |       |   | REL3
